1 RETURN

   Ends the commands a GOSUB ran, going on after the GOSUB.

   Format

     RETURN [status]

2 Parameter

 status

   An expression, which becomes $STATUS; a failure's message is shown,
   as EXIT's is.  Without one, $STATUS is %X10000001.

2 Description

   A RETURN with no GOSUB is DCL-W-BADRET.  At the terminal, RETURN
   shows nothing: with a status, $STATUS becomes it, and without one
   $STATUS is marked as shown.  See GOSUB.
